      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Consider defining named constants for the region array capacity (`16`) and the default `MPU_TYPE` register value (`0x00000800`), along with a `MOCK_MPU_DEFAULT` compound-literal initializer macro (matching the pattern in `common/mock/README.md`):\n\n```c\n#define MOCK_MPU_MAX_REGIONS 16\n#define MOCK_MPU_DEFAULT_TYPE 0x00000800 /* 8 unified regions */\n\nstruct mock_mpu_state {\n\tuint32_t type;\n\tuint32_t ctrl;\n\tuint32_t base[MOCK_MPU_MAX_REGIONS];\n\tuint32_t rasr[MOCK_MPU_MAX_REGIONS];\n};\n\n#define MOCK_MPU_DEFAULT \\\n\t((struct mock_mpu_state){ .type \u003d MOCK_MPU_DEFAULT_TYPE })\n```\n\nThis avoids repeating `16` here and `0x00000800` in `common/mock/mpu_mock.c`, allows `mock_mpu_reset()` to simply assign `mock_mpu \u003d MOCK_MPU_DEFAULT;`, and lets `mpu_update_region()` also bound-check `region \u003e\u003d MOCK_MPU_MAX_REGIONS` in case a test overrides `mock_mpu.type` with a region count larger than the mock arrays.\n\nOther locations:\n* **`common/mock/mpu_mock.c` (Lines 18-26, 34)**: Initialize `mock_mpu \u003d MOCK_MPU_DEFAULT;`, reset with `mock_mpu \u003d MOCK_MPU_DEFAULT;`, and check `region \u003e\u003d MOCK_MPU_MAX_REGIONS`.\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/ee04c723-4b62-475f-84ee-92ea177552d0)",
